page RecipePublishCustomElements(path: "/recipes/publish-custom-elements", title: "Publish components as custom elements — Recipes", description: "To use your components from another framework or a plain page, build them as custom elements.") {
    RecipeShell("Publish components as custom elements", summary: "To use your components from another framework or a plain page, build them as custom elements. Name the components in `build.elements`:  ```json \{ \"build\": \{ \"output_type\": \"elements\", \"elements\": [\"PriceTag\", \"Rating\"] \} \} ```  Each name becomes a standard custom element. `PriceTag` is `<price-tag>`. A one-word component gets a prefix, so its tag has the hyphen a custom element needs: `Rating` is `<wf-rating>`. The build writes `elements.js`, `styles.css`, and a page that lists the tags it published.  This HTML places a published component on any page:  ```html <script src=\"/elements.js\" defer></script> <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\">  <price-tag label=\"Pro\" amount=\"29\" sale></price-tag> ```  How a published element behaves:  - **An attribute is a prop.** It is read when the element is connected, and again whenever it changes. A `Number` prop is read as a number, and a `Map` or a list as JSON. - **A `Bool` prop is true when the attribute is present**, as HTML reads `disabled`, and false when it is `=\"false\"`, so a framework that writes the string still works. - **An event the component declares** is dispatched as a `CustomEvent` that bubbles. - **What the component created goes** when the element leaves the document.  React, Vue, Svelte, Angular, Rails, WordPress and a plain page can all place a tag. That is why WebFluent publishes custom elements rather than an adapter per framework: the interface every framework shares is the web platform itself.", outputs: [], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Call WF from a script", to: "/recipes/call-wf-from-a-script"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Call your own JavaScript", to: "/recipes/call-your-own-script"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Draw a chart from a library", to: "/recipes/chart-from-a-library")], source: "md-docs/recipes/publish-custom-elements.md", how: false, hasVariations: false) {
    }
}
